    "body": "## Summary\n\nBoth WebViews the app creates set `mixedContentMode = MIXED_CONTENT_ALWAYS_ALLOW`: the one each AI service is shown in (`updateWebViewSettings`) and the temporary one used for `window.open` (`CustomWebChromeClient.onCreateWindow`). That lets an HTTPS page load scripts, frames or images over plain HTTP, which anyone on the same network can read or replace. I came across it while running a static analysis tool (Semgrep) over Android apps.\n\nThe services the app opens are all served over HTTPS, so this sets both WebViews to `MIXED_CONTENT_NEVER_ALLOW`, which is also what WebView uses by default for apps targeting Android 5.0 or later.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `app/src/main/java/com/foss/aihub/ui/webview/WebViewUtils.kt`: `MIXED_CONTENT_ALWAYS_ALLOW` → `MIXED_CONTENT_NEVER_ALLOW` in `updateWebViewSettings`.\n- `app/src/main/java/com/foss/aihub/ui/webview/WebChromeClient.kt`: the same for the WebView created in `onCreateWindow`.\n\n## How was this tested?\n\nThe project builds (`assembleDebug`). I didn't add a test: the setting only takes effect inside a real WebView, so a unit test would only restate the constant.\n\n## Additional context\n\nI'm an undergraduate Computer Engineering student at the University of Brasília (UnB), and this contribution is part of a research project involving static analysis of Android apps.\n\nI'm happy to adjust the implementation to better match the project's architecture, coding conventions, or maintainers' recommendations.\n",
